(1) We consider the coordinate system of an observer at infinity $(t,r,\theta,\phi)$. At time $t=t_0$, a spacecraft is at point $A$. Draw the trajectory of the spacecraft from $t=t_0$ to $t=\infty$ assuming that the spacecraft travels at the constant velocity $v=0.999999999c$ ($c=$ speed of light) with $dr/dt>0$. Is the trajectory of the spacecraft a time-like geodesic? [8 Points]

(2) Let us now assume that at time $t=t_0$ the spacecraft is still at point $A$ but it is orbiting around the star $S$. The orbit is circular $(dr/dt=0)$ and remains circular. Draw the trajectory of the spacecraft from $t=t_0$ to $t=\infty$. [8 Points]

(3) Suppose that the spacecraft at point $A$ emits an electromagnetic signal. Draw the trajectory of such an electromagnetic signal. [8 Points]

3. (60 Points) Let us consider the following line element
\begin{equation}
ds^2=-dt^2+a^2\left(\frac{dr^2}{1-r^2}+r^2d\theta^2+r^2\sin^2\theta d\phi^2\right),
\end{equation}
where $a=a(t)=\sqrt{t-t^2}$ is a function of $t$.

(1) Is this a universe filled with matter, radiation, or vacuum energy? Please explain how you can infer the matter content or why you cannot answer this question. [10 Points]

(2) Write the energy $E$ and the axial component of the angular momentum $L_z$ of a test-particle in this spacetime. Are $E$ and $L_z$ constants of motion? [5 Points]

(3) Assuming that the spacetime has a trivial topology, is the $3$-volume finite or infinite? [5 Points]

(4) At the time $t=0.1$, an atom emits a photon of energy $E=5\,\mathrm{eV}$. What is the photon energy at the time $t=0.3$? Can a photon be blueshifted in this spacetime and why? [8 Points]

(5) Does the spacetime have an ergoregion? In the case of positive answer, where? [8 Points]

(6) Does the spacetime have curvature singularities? In the case of positive answer, where? [8 Points]

(7) Write the vierbeins $E^\mu{}_{(\alpha)}$. [8 Points]

(8) Is the spacetime asymptotically flat? In the case of positive answer, draw its Penrose diagram. [8 Points]